            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>An intravascular device for deflecting emboli comprising: a frame, an embolic filter attached to said frame, wherein the frame defines the shape of the filter and the frame is suitable to be held in contact with both an ascending and a descending aorta, an upper stabilizer, and a lower stabilizer located below a horizontal plane of said filter, wherein one of the upper or lower stabilizer comprises a wire configured to run along the horizontal plane of the filter and exert a force on the frame and/or the filter when deployed in an aorta of a subject, wherein the wire comprises a tether and the lower stabilizer comprises the tether and the tether is configured to exert a force below the horizontal plane of said filter or the upper stabilizer comprises the tether and the tether is configured to exert a force above the horizontal plane of the filter.</p>
            </abstract>
